  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q12",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "For the polynomial $P(x)=(a+1)x^3+(b-7)x^2+c+5$, find $a$, $b$, $c$ given that:\n\nThe degree is 2, $P(x)$ is monic, and the constant term is $-1$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=-1,\\ b=8,\\ c=-6$.",
      "worked": "The degree is 2, so the coefficient of $x^3$ is zero. Since the polynomial is monic, the coefficient of $x^2$ is 1. The constant term is $-1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}a+1&=0\\\\a&=-1\\\\b-7&=1\\\\b&=8\\\\c+5&=-1\\\\c&=-6\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 24
  },
